### What this section does and does not tell you

The exporter rejects any metric datagram that is empty, missing required fields, in an unknown format, from an unknown producer, numerically invalid, or carries an unsupported event. Rejection happens **before any business mutation**, so a rejected datagram never partially updates a metric. Rejections are counted below.

**Zero rejected metric datagrams does not prove every producer event was delivered.** The MVP has no producer epoch, sequence number, or replay cache, so there is no delivery-completeness measurement and no telemetry-reliability percentage:

- a datagram lost in transit is **invisible** here;
- a duplicated otherwise-valid datagram may be applied again;
- exporter restart resets all counters and gauges, and a gauge only recovers when a later producer event carries absolute state;
- telemetry-send failure never changes or rolls back the protocol outcome.

When evidence is incomplete, the affected reconciliation result is `INCONCLUSIVE` — not a pass. See "Explicitly deferred hardening" in `METRICS.md`.
